  "line": "The Jordan is the main river of the land of Israel, where God opened the water for His people and where Jesus was baptized.",
  "moments": [
    {
      "title": "Israel Crosses on Dry Ground",
      "text": "When the priests carrying the ark touched the Jordan, the flowing water stood still. All Israel crossed on dry ground near Jericho.",
      "passage": "Joshua 3:13-17"
    },
    {
      "title": "Twelve Stones from the River",
      "text": "The LORD told Joshua to have twelve men, one from each tribe, take stones from the middle of the Jordan. The stones were a memorial of how the waters were cut off.",
      "passage": "Joshua 4:1-9"
    },
    {
      "title": "Elisha Takes Up the Cloak",
      "text": "After Elijah went up into heaven, Elisha picked up Elijah's cloak and struck the Jordan. The waters parted and he crossed over.",
      "passage": "2 Kings 2:11-15"
    },
    {
      "title": "Naaman Washes and Is Healed",
      "text": "Elisha told Naaman to wash seven times in the Jordan. Naaman did it, and his flesh was restored like that of a little child.",
      "passage": "2 Kings 5:10-14"
    },
    {
      "title": "Jesus Is Baptized",
      "text": "Jesus came from Galilee to the Jordan to be baptized by John. The Spirit of God came down like a dove, and a voice from heaven called Him God's beloved Son.",
      "passage": "Matthew 3:13-17"
    }
  ],
